title Fold S -- record_the_dispute, and the second tier-owner an accessor brought home
prompt Take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, Standfast on reds first, and send it.
think Standfast came first. The REDS ledger reads 110 rows, and every row with an open finding carries a closure beside it -- REDS %110 closed on the same lap it was booked, the prose-count rule now a property rather than a habit. No agent-closable red stood open, so the line was clear for constructive work.
think The running thread is the Caravan ladder fold arc, and the last three recommends agree on the queue. Fold R named record_the_dispute the better crux over provision_notes -- thirty-two rungs against twenty-four, and provision_notes at ninety-one lines stays the body most likely to reach a rung's own wire, which is what keeps a body home.
think Fold O's lesson held again: hash the family before folding it. Thirty-three files declare record_the_dispute where the queue printed thirty-two, and the thirty-third was not a stranger -- dispute.rye OWNS the disputing tier, so it reached its own report directly where all thirty-two above reach it through disputing_of. Five differences, every one the same difference. This is fold R's absentee, read a second time.
think A three-line identity accessor folds all sixty-one, which is fold M's lesson holding for the fourth time. dispute.rye gained pub fn disputing_of(report_out: *Report) *Report returning the report itself, and its sixty-one folded with the rest.
think The widening survey named forty-nine: couriering_of private in twenty-five rungs, disputing_of private in twenty-four. Fourteen of the sixteen symbols the body names stood public in all thirty-three already, paid for by the folds before it. Every couriering_of and disputing_of body is a distinct text, since each reaches a different depth, so the widening split no family and handed back no carry.
think Both arithmetics were closed by measurement rather than assumption. The queue measured 1891 carried -- thirty-one copies, since dispute.rye stood distinct and carried nothing. The new delegate family is thirty-three identical eight-line bodies carrying 32 x 8 = 256. 1891 - 256 = 1635, and the meter measured 127567 -> 125932, a fall of exactly 1635.
obs The second kind of absentee is now the expected kind, not the surprise. Fold R found a tier-owner standing outside its own family; fold S found another the very next lap. A meter that keys bodies by exact text can never see this, because the difference it reads as distinctness is the very fact of ownership. Reading past the queue has paid on three consecutive laps.
obs The disk arithmetic closes independently and names its own artifact. Thirty-two rungs shed fifty-three lines apiece for 1696, dispute.rye shed forty-three -- fifty-three out and ten back for its accessor -- and ladder_checks.rye took ninety-one, for a net of 1648 over the real rung files. A naive tracked-line count reads 366543 -> 365063, a fall of 1480, because caravan/parse_int.rye and caravan/tally_copy.rye are tracked symlinks whose target text wc follows and git show does not. The 168-line gap is the symlink, named rather than left to drift.
obs A fold pays its successors, and the ledger of that claim keeps lengthening. Fold P found five of five symbols already public; fold R found fourteen of sixteen; fold S found the same fourteen and needed only the two accessors. The arc's public surface is converging on what the harness actually names.
