file caravan/ladder_checks.rye the harness gains record_the_dispute as one comptime body over thirty-three rungs, its doc naming both the thirty-third and the widening cost
file caravan/dispute.rye the tier owner gains a three-line identity accessor so its own sixty-one folds with the rest
file caravan/abate.rye thirty-two rungs each trade a sixty-one-line body for an eight-line delegate; abate.rye stands for them all in this field
file tools/fixtures/caravan_ladder_carry_scan.sh the ceiling comes down 127600 -> 126000, and the fold ledger in its header gains this lap
file tools/caravan_ladder_carry_witness.rish the meter repins to 125932 across 10197 copies, and the queue's second name moves to graft_promised_reach
recommend keep-going The queue's lead is ungated and now stands alone: provision_notes at 2093 across 24 rungs, with graft_promised_reach at 1763 across 42 and hear_the_reader at 1728 across 33 behind it. graft_promised_reach is the better crux -- forty-two rungs against twenty-four, and provision_notes at ninety-one lines stays the body most likely to reach a rung's own wire. Hash the family before folding it, and read the absentees for which of the two kinds they are; a tier-owner standing apart has now appeared on two consecutive laps and should be looked for rather than stumbled on. The one gate worth Keaton's eye stays small and unchanged: jinja2 and ply on the pier's Python environment open the seL4 generated headers in a single step.
